{%- doc -%}
  A longer annotation that runs the full width of the sheet, with a coloured bar down its
  left edge. On a physical proof sheet this is the grease pencil scrawl in the margin: the
  reason a frame was kept, what went wrong with the ones either side of it, or the note to
  push the next roll a stop.

  Unlike the frame and caption blocks, this one deliberately breaks the grid. The CSS sets
  it to span every column, so wherever a merchant drops it in the block list, it lands as a
  full width band rather than sitting in a single cell. That is what makes it read as a
  margin note about the frames around it rather than another item in the sequence.

  This block is specific to the Contact Sheet. The full width span assumes it is inside a
  CSS grid, so placing it in a section that lays blocks out any other way would leave it
  looking like an ordinary paragraph.

  note_accent is a merchant colour that feeds the left bar through a CSS variable, so
  different notes on the same sheet can be colour coded the way a photographer uses
  different pencils for keeps, rejects and reprints.
{%- enddoc -%}

{% assign block_settings = block.settings %}

<div
  class="exposure-note"
  style="--exposure-note-accent: {{ block_settings.note_accent }};"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="exposure-note__body">
    {{ block_settings.note }}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .exposure-note {
    /* Spans every column of the parent grid regardless of how many columns the section
       is set to, which is what turns this from a cell into a band. */
    grid-column: 1 / -1;

    padding: var(--padding-sm) var(--padding-md);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--exposure-note-accent, currentColor);
    background: var(--contact-sheet-line, rgb(128 128 128 / 0.08));
  }

  .exposure-note__body {
    font-size: var(--font-paragraph-small--size);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .exposure-note__body > :first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .exposure-note__body > :last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.exposure_note",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "note",
      "label": "t:settings.exposure_note",
      "default": "<p>Frames 12 through 15 were shot into the light on purpose. The flare is the point, not a mistake — this is why the stock is worth the money.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "note_accent",
      "label": "t:settings.color",
      "default": "#ffcf8f"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:names.exposure_note",
      "category": "t:categories.storytelling"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
